// Views. Navigation: 1 · Context -> 2 · Containers -> 3 · Components (hub ADR-0015).

views {
  style element.tag = #planned {
    border dashed
    opacity 70%
  }

  view index {
    title '1 · Context / @stateforge-labs/herdr-sdk'
    order 1
    description '''
      Who uses the library and what does it talk to? voice-hub (Effect), atalaya-bridge (Node, Promise) and scripts; herdr is the
      only system the library calls. **Click the library** for its entry points.
    '''
    include owner, herdr, voiceHub, atalaya, scripts
    include lib with {
      navigateTo entries
    }
    rank source {
      owner
    }
    rank sink {
      herdr
    }
    autoLayout LeftRight
  }

  view entries of lib {
    title '2 · Containers / @stateforge-labs/herdr-sdk'
    order 1
    description '''
      Which entry points exist and who imports which? One subpath export each (/admin adds destructive and server-control methods); the core has zero runtime dependencies, only /effect
      needs effect as a peer, test-kit and the generator/drift tooling (slate) never reach a production bundle.
      **Decisions:** HERDR-ADR-0003, HERDR-ADR-0004, HERDR-ADR-0005, HERDR-ADR-0008, HERDR-ADR-0009
    '''
    include *
    include herdr, voiceHub, atalaya, scripts, owner
    include lib.core with {
      navigateTo coreComponents
    }
    include lib.effectEntry with {
      navigateTo effectComponents
    }
    rank source {
      voiceHub,
      atalaya,
      scripts,
      owner
    }
    rank sink {
      herdr
    }
    autoLayout LeftRight
  }

  view coreComponents of lib.core {
    title '3 · Components / Core client'
    order 1
    description '''
      How does a call reach herdr? namespace client -> wire (rpc, framing, envelope, errors, protocol policy) -> unix socket; scoped
      clients narrow the namespace tree; subscribe and held connections each open a dedicated connection; watch adds snapshot, replay and resubscribe.
      **Decisions:** HERDR-ADR-0002, HERDR-ADR-0005, HERDR-ADR-0007
    '''
    include *
    include herdr
    rank sink {
      herdr
    }
    autoLayout LeftRight
  }

  view effectComponents of lib.effectEntry {
    title '3 · Components / Effect client'
    order 2
    description '''
      How does the Effect entry wrap the core? Layers provide the Herdr service, which fails with the hub tagged errors; Stream subscribe
      and watchPaneSet wrap the core subscription with acquireRelease and resubscribe.
      **Decisions:** HERDR-ADR-0004, HERDR-ADR-0007
    '''
    include *
    include lib.core.namespaces, lib.core.subscribe
    include voiceHub
    autoLayout LeftRight
  }
}
